---
// Alternative landing page for Google Ads testing (noindex, not in nav/sitemap).
// Positioning test: ownership/learning-first, "Stop paying for intelligence twice".
// Copy style: short stacked lines, minimal prose walls.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="KYDE, Stop Paying for Intelligence Twice"
  description="Own the intelligence your company creates. KYDE is the behavioral system of record for autonomous work: every interaction routed through it stays inside your tenant and lands in one hash-chained record, with zero code changes."
  noindex={true}
>
  <Navbar />
  <main>

    <!-- ══════════ HERO · exhaust capture loop ══════════ -->
    <section class="dark-island relative overflow-hidden min-h-[92vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-20 border-b border-white/10 bg-bg-0">
      <canvas id="lp-exhaust" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none bg-gradient-to-r from-bg-0 via-bg-0/50 to-transparent"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-transparent to-bg-0"></div>

      <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 w-full py-24">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h1 class="hero-h1 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl text-white uppercase tracking-tight leading-[1.02] mb-8">
            Stop paying for<br />intelligence twice.
          </h1>
          <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-white font-semibold leading-snug mb-6">
            Own the intelligence your company creates.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-white/70 uppercase tracking-[0.12em] leading-snug mb-8">
            The trust boundary and learning infrastructure for enterprise AI.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-white/50 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-10">
            KYDE intercepts every interaction before it crosses your trust boundary, keeps your operational intelligence inside your own tenant, and turns it into a long-term enterprise asset, with zero code changes.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-12 font-mono text-sm">
            <span class="text-live">$</span> <span class="text-white/50">export OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://gateway.kyde.intranet/v1</span>
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
            <button
              onclick="openModal()"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-white/40 text-white px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:border-white hover:bg-white/10 transition-all"
            >
              Talk to Us →
            </button>
            <a
              href="/starter"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white text-cta-ink px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:bg-cta-hover transition-all"
            >
              Start Free →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 01 · REVERSE INFORMATION PARADOX ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-line-0 bg-bg-1">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="mb-16">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-line-0 pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-1">01 · The Reverse Information Paradox</span></div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-ink-0 leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-16 max-w-4xl">
          Every company using AI is creating a new asset.
        </h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-20 mb-20 items-start">
          <div class="space-y-1.5 text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug">
            <p class="text-ink-0">Every employee correction.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/80">Every successful workflow.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/65">Every failed tool call.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/50">Every retry.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/40">Every evaluation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="md:pt-2">
            <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed mb-6">
              Every one of these interactions teaches an AI system how your business operates. This is your operational intelligence. Today, most companies unknowingly give it away.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-2"><span class="text-ink-0">You pay once</span><span class="text-ink-1"> through API fees.</span></p>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed"><span class="text-ink-0">You pay again</span><span class="text-ink-1"> by shipping your operational intelligence to external model providers.</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-line-0 bg-bg-2 p-8 md:p-10 mb-20 max-w-3xl">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gold mb-5">The Reverse Information Paradox</p>
          <p class="text-xl text-ink-0 leading-relaxed">
            Over time, vendors learn more about your business than you learn about their models.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- FIG.1 · who owns the learning? -->
        <div class="relative border border-line-0 bg-bg-0 p-8 md:p-14 mb-20">
          <span class="fig-label absolute top-4 left-5">FIG.1 · Who owns the learning?</span>
          <div id="lp-fig1" class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr] gap-10 md:gap-14 pt-8 items-start">
            <div>
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-2 mb-6">What leaves your company</p>
              <ul class="space-y-3">
                {["Prompts", "Corrections", "Tool traces", "Agent trajectories", "Evaluations", "Operational workflows"].map((item) => (
                  <li class="lp-fig1-out flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-sm text-ink-0 opacity-0 -translate-x-2 transition-all duration-500">
                    <span class="text-live">→</span>{item}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="hidden md:flex flex-col items-center justify-center self-stretch pt-10" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="w-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-line-1 to-transparent"></div>
              <span class="font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/25 py-4 [writing-mode:vertical-rl]">Trust Boundary</span>
              <div class="w-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-line-1 to-transparent"></div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-2 mb-6">What comes back</p>
              <ul class="space-y-3">
                {["Black-box reasoning", "No ownership", "No transparency", "No reusable knowledge"].map((item) => (
                  <li class="lp-fig1-back flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-sm text-alert/70 opacity-0 translate-x-2 transition-all duration-500">
                    <span>✕</span>{item}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-ink-0 mb-8">KYDE changes the direction, at the trust boundary.</p>
          <div class="space-y-1.5 text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug">
            <p class="text-ink-0/60">Your models improve.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/80">Your company learns.</p>
            <p class="text-live">Your operational intelligence stays yours.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 02 · ARCHITECTURE ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-line-0 bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="mb-16">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-line-0 pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-1">02 · Architecture</span></div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-ink-0 leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-10 max-w-4xl">
          One gateway. Every agent.<br />Zero code changes.
        </h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-20 mb-20 items-start">
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">
            Every capability KYDE provides, security, governance, compliance, cost optimization and organizational learning, comes from controlling a single stream of agent interactions at the trust boundary. KYDE does not run inside your agents. It sits in the critical path between your organization and every AI provider. <span class="text-ink-0">This is operational sovereignty by architecture.</span>
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-1.5 text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug md:pt-1">
            <p class="text-ink-0/40">Every request.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/55">Every tool call.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/70">Every response.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/85">Every correction.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0">Everything flows through one gateway.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- FIG.2 · the critical path, live -->
        <div class="relative border border-line-0 bg-bg-1 p-6 md:p-10 mb-20">
          <span class="fig-label absolute top-4 left-5 z-10">FIG.2 · The critical path, live</span>
          <svg id="lp-flow" viewBox="0 0 800 440" class="w-full h-auto pt-6" aria-hidden="true">
            <!-- agent nodes -->
            {[
              { x: 75,  label: "claude" },
              { x: 205, label: "gpt-5" },
              { x: 335, label: "gemini" },
              { x: 465, label: "langchain" },
              { x: 595, label: "open-src" },
              { x: 725, label: "mcp-tools" },
            ].map(({ x, label }) => (
              <g>
                <rect x={x - 32} y={30} width={64} height={30} fill="none" stroke="#2E2E2E" stroke-width="1" />
                <text x={x} y={49} text-anchor="middle" fill="rgba(242,242,242,0.55)" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.06em;">{label}</text>
                <line x1={x} y1={60} x2={400} y2={190} stroke="#1F1F1F" stroke-width="1" />
              </g>
            ))}
            <!-- gateway -->
            <rect x="270" y="190" width="260" height="56" fill="#0C0C0C" stroke="#F2F2F2" stroke-opacity="0.5" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <rect x="276" y="196" width="248" height="44" fill="none" stroke="#1F1F1F" stroke-width="1" />
            <text x="400" y="215" text-anchor="middle" fill="#F2F2F2" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;">KYDE GATEWAY</text>
            <text x="400" y="232" text-anchor="middle" fill="rgba(242,242,242,0.35)" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.12em;">POLICY · IDENTITY · AUDIT · LEARNING</text>
            <!-- output lanes -->
            {[
              { x: 140, n: "Security",   d: "Prevent" },
              { x: 400, n: "Governance", d: "Prove" },
              { x: 660, n: "Learning",   d: "Compound" },
            ].map(({ x, n, d }) => (
              <g>
                <line x1={400} y1={246} x2={x} y2={330} stroke="#1F1F1F" stroke-width="1" />
                <rect x={x - 90} y={330} width={180} height={72} fill="none" stroke="#2E2E2E" stroke-width="1" />
                <text x={x} y={362} text-anchor="middle" fill="#F2F2F2" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0.08em;">{n}</text>
                <text x={x} y={382} text-anchor="middle" fill="rgba(242,242,242,0.35)" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.2em;">{d.toUpperCase()}</text>
              </g>
            ))}
            <g id="lp-flow-dots"></g>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-2 mb-8">The Gateway</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          {[
            { k: "Zero code changes",  v: "Redirect your SDKs to the KYDE Gateway." },
            { k: "Provider agnostic",  v: "Works with OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and open-source models." },
            { k: "Sub-100ms latency",  v: "An optimized interception pipeline built for production workloads." },
            { k: "MCP native",         v: "Supports the Model Context Protocol out of the box." },
          ].map(({ k, v }) => (
            <div class="border border-line-0 bg-bg-1 p-6">
              <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-0 mb-3">{k}</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">{v}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 03 · ONE INFRASTRUCTURE. THREE OUTCOMES. ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-line-0 bg-bg-1">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="mb-16">
          <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-line-0 pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-1">03 · One infrastructure. Three outcomes.</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-ink-0 leading-snug max-w-3xl">
          Every interaction crossing the trust boundary creates a cryptographically signed record.
          <span class="text-ink-1">The same stream powers three independent capabilities.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ SECURITY ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-line-0 bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-alert mb-8">Security</p>
        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink-0 leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-10 max-w-3xl">
          Prevent what must never happen.
        </h2>
        <div class="mb-20 max-w-2xl space-y-2">
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">Traditional audit systems explain failures after they occur. <span class="text-ink-0">KYDE prevents them before they happen.</span></p>
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">Every request is evaluated against deterministic policies before it reaches the model provider.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
          <!-- FIG.3 · live intercept -->
          <div class="dark-island relative border border-line-0 bg-bg-1">
            <span class="fig-label absolute -top-7 left-0">FIG.3 · Live intercept</span>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-white/8 px-4 py-3">
              <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-alert/40"></span>
              <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-warn/40"></span>
              <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-live/40"></span>
              <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-[10px] text-white/20">gateway · intercept feed</span>
              <span id="lp-intercept-policy" class="ml-auto font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-widest text-white/30 border border-line-0 px-2 py-0.5">deny-by-default</span>
            </div>
            <div id="lp-intercept" class="p-6 font-mono text-xs leading-loose h-[340px] overflow-hidden"></div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-2 mb-6">Active protection</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-8">
              {[
                "Data Loss Prevention (DLP)",
                "PII redaction",
                "Intellectual property protection",
                "Tool access policies",
                "Loop detection",
                "Cost guardrails",
              ].map((item) => (
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 border border-line-0 bg-bg-1 px-4 py-3.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink-0">
                  <span class="text-alert">✕</span>{item}
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">
              Sensitive information never crosses your trust boundary unless your policies explicitly allow it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ GOVERNANCE ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-line-0 bg-bg-1">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold mb-8">Governance</p>
        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink-0 leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-10 max-w-3xl">
          Prove what happened.
        </h2>
        <div class="mb-20 max-w-2xl space-y-2">
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">Vendor logs live on vendor infrastructure. <span class="text-ink-0">They are not independent evidence.</span></p>
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">KYDE writes a hash-chained audit trail before any token crosses your trust boundary, so altering one entry breaks every entry after it.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- FIG.4 · the chain defends itself -->
        <div class="relative border border-line-0 bg-bg-0 p-8 md:p-12 mb-16 overflow-hidden">
          <span class="fig-label absolute top-4 left-5">FIG.4 · The chain defends itself</span>
          <div id="lp-chain" class="flex items-center gap-0 pt-8 pb-2 font-mono text-xs overflow-hidden whitespace-nowrap"></div>
          <p id="lp-chain-status" class="mt-6 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-white/30">Appending entries…</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
          <div>
            <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-2 mb-6">Every interaction is</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              {[
                "Cryptographically signed",
                "Hash-chained",
                "Tamper-evident",
                "Independently verifiable",
              ].map((item) => (
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 border border-line-0 bg-bg-2 px-4 py-3.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink-0">
                  <span class="text-live">✓</span>{item}
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed md:pt-10">
            Generate evidence for the agent layer of GDPR, DORA, NIS-2 and EU AI Act duties, directly from production traffic. It does not discharge those duties on its own.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ LEARNING ══════════ -->
    <section class="border-t border-line-0 bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-live mb-8">Learning</p>
        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink-0 leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-10 max-w-3xl">
          Own the asset you are already creating.
        </h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-20 mb-20 items-start">
          <div class="space-y-1.5 text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug">
            <p class="text-ink-0">Every correction contains knowledge.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/75">Every successful workflow contains knowledge.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/55">Every failed trajectory contains knowledge.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-0/40">Every evaluation contains knowledge.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="md:pt-2 space-y-2">
            <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">Most companies discard this information or unintentionally transfer it to their AI vendors. <span class="text-ink-0">KYDE captures it inside your trust boundary.</span></p>
            <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">Your operational intelligence becomes an enterprise asset that compounds over time.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- FIG.5 · rented vs. owned -->
        <div class="relative border border-line-0 bg-bg-1 p-8 md:p-12 mb-16">
          <span class="fig-label absolute top-4 left-5">FIG.5 · Rented vs. owned intelligence</span>
          <svg id="lp-curve" viewBox="0 0 760 300" class="w-full h-auto pt-8" aria-hidden="true">
            <line x1="40" y1="260" x2="740" y2="260" stroke="#1F1F1F" stroke-width="1" />
            <line x1="40" y1="20" x2="40" y2="260" stroke="#1F1F1F" stroke-width="1" />
            <text x="740" y="278" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(242,242,242,0.3)" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.15em;">TIME →</text>
            <text x="30" y="24" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(242,242,242,0.3)" transform="rotate(-90 30 24)" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.15em;">INSTITUTIONAL INTELLIGENCE</text>
            <!-- rented: flat, resets at every contract switch -->
            <path id="lp-curve-rented" d="M40 236 L200 232 L200 244 L380 240 L380 250 L560 246 L560 254 L740 251" fill="none" stroke="rgba(242,242,242,0.3)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
            <text x="450" y="225" fill="rgba(242,242,242,0.35)" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">RENTED · resets with every vendor switch</text>
            <!-- owned: compounding curve -->
            <path id="lp-curve-owned" d="M40 256 C 220 252, 380 240, 500 190 C 590 152, 660 96, 740 40" fill="none" stroke="#3DDC84" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="500" y="120" fill="#3DDC84" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono Variable',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">OWNED · your ledger compounds</text>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-16">
          {[
            { t: "Better guardrails", d: "Use real production behavior to continuously improve prompts, routing logic, policies and evaluations. Your AI infrastructure becomes safer with every interaction." },
            { t: "Smaller, smarter models", d: "Fine-tune lightweight open-source models on your own operational knowledge. The large foundation model becomes rented compute. Your specialized intelligence remains yours." },
            { t: "Better buying decisions", d: "Measure success rate, retry chains, cost per completed task, and human intervention. Stop buying AI on benchmarks and marketing. Negotiate with your own operational data." },
          ].map(({ t, d }) => (
            <div class="border border-line-0 bg-bg-1 p-8">
              <p class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-0 mb-3">{t}</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">{d}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-12 items-center">
          <!-- scorecard -->
          <div class="border border-line-0 bg-bg-1 overflow-x-auto">
            <div class="border-b border-line-0 px-5 py-3.5 flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-1">Example scorecard · last 30 days</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-widest text-live border border-live/30 px-1.5 py-0.5">Live</span>
            </div>
            <table class="w-full font-mono text-xs">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-line-0 text-ink-2 uppercase tracking-widest text-[10px]">
                  <th class="text-left px-5 py-3">Agent</th>
                  <th class="text-left px-5 py-3">Provider</th>
                  <th class="text-left px-5 py-3">Cost/Task</th>
                  <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 w-32">Success</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-line-0 text-ink-1">
                {[
                  { a: "agent:support-02", p: "OpenAI",      c: "$0.12", s: 87 },
                  { a: "agent:proc-7",     p: "Anthropic",   c: "$0.41", s: 64 },
